.* SETUP: the task menu for customizing the system.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='SETUP'.
:KEYL NAME=MENUKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.F1=Help
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION='CMD CALL QCMD'.F9=Command line
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=SETUP HELP=HLPSETUP KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.Customize Your System, Users, and Devices
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.To select an option, type its number below and press Enter:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD WRKSYSVAL'.Change system options
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='MENU CLEANUP'.Cleanup tasks
:MENUI OPTION=3 ACTION='MENU POWER'.Power on and off tasks
:MENUI OPTION=4 ACTION='MENU DISKTASKS'.Disk space tasks
:MENUI OPTION=5 ACTION='MENU BACKUP'.Backup tasks
:MENUI OPTION=11 ACTION='CMD ?CHGUSRPRF USRPRF(QSECOFR)'.Change passwords for IBM-supplied users
:MENUI OPTION=20 ACTION='MENU CMNCFG'.Communications configuration tasks
:EMENU.
:BOTINST.Type a menu option below
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPSETUP.Customize Your System, Users, and Devices - Help
:P.Setting the system up the way this site wants it: options, cleanup,
power, backup and the passwords of the shipped profiles.
:P.Type an option number and press Enter. F9 opens a command line, F3
leaves the menu and F12 returns to the one before it.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
